The bug was introduced by changing the overflow detection from checking for exact maximum/minimum values (16'b1111_1111_1111_1111 and 16'b0) to only checking the MSB (count[15]). This could miss some overflow cases because:
1. When counting up, it will wrap around when MSB becomes 1 (at 32768), not at the actual maximum value (65535)
2. When counting down, it will wrap around when MSB becomes 0 (at 32767), not at the actual minimum value (0)
This creates an incorrect wrap-around behavior where the counter wraps at half the intended range.
