The change replaces all `<=` non-blocking assignments with `=` blocking assignments. This creates a potential race condition because:
1. The Q updates will happen immediately in the current time step
2. Any downstream logic that reads Q in the same always block (or in other always blocks triggered by the same clock edge) will see the new value immediately
3. This can lead to simulation mismatches between RTL and gate-level simulations
4. The behavior becomes dependent on the order of always block execution

The code remains syntactically valid and compilable while introducing the race condition as specified.
