Design a 64-bit linear feedback shift register (LFSR) module with synchronous reset. The module should implement the following behavior:

1. On the positive edge of the clock (clk), the register content Q[63:0] should shift right by 1 bit
2. The new MSB (Q[63]) should be:
   - 1 if the shifted-out LSB (Q[0]) was 0
   - 0 if the shifted-out LSB (Q[0]) was 1
3. When the active-low reset (rst_n) is asserted (0), the register should synchronously clear to all 0s
4. All operations should occur on the rising clock edge

Inputs:
- clk: system clock (posedge triggered)
- rst_n: active-low synchronous reset

Output:
- Q: 64-bit register output

The module should be purely sequential with no combinational paths. Assume all inputs are glitch-free and meet setup/hold times.
QUESTION END
