Design a 64-bit linear feedback shift register (LFSR) module with the following specifications:

Inputs:
- clk: positive edge-triggered clock input
- rst_n: active-low synchronous reset (resets on rising clock edge when low)

Output:
- Q: 64-bit register output

Behavior:
1. When rst_n is low, Q should reset to all zeros on the next rising clock edge
2. When rst_n is high, Q should shift right by 1 bit each clock cycle
3. The new MSB (bit 63) should be:
   - 1 if the outgoing LSB (bit 0) was 0
   - 0 if the outgoing LSB (bit 0) was 1
4. All other bits should shift right normally (Q[62:0] → Q[63:1])

The module should be purely synchronous to the positive clock edge and respond to the reset signal. Do not implement any additional features like seed loading or parallel input.
QUESTION END
