- Three 1-bit outputs:
  * A_greater: high when A[1:0] > B[1:0]
  * A_equal: high when A[1:0] == B[1:0]
  * A_less: high when A[1:0] < B[1:0]

The comparison should be unsigned and should only consider bits [1:0] of each input (ignore the MSB). All outputs should be combinational and update immediately when inputs change. Only the two LSBs of each input should affect the outputs, regardless of the MSB values.

