Inputs:
- clk: System clock (positive edge triggered)
- rst: Active-low asynchronous reset
- fetch[1:0]: Control signal indicating which part of instruction to store (01 for first part, 10 for second part)
- data[7:0]: Input data to be stored

Outputs:
- ins[2:0]: Upper 3 bits of the first instruction part
- ad1[4:0]: Lower 5 bits of the first instruction part
- ad2[7:0]: Complete second instruction part

Behavior:
1. On reset (rst=0), clear all internal storage registers
2. On rising clock edges when rst=1:
   - When fetch=01, store data in the first instruction register
   - When fetch=10, store data in the second instruction register
   - For other fetch values, maintain current register values
3. The outputs should continuously reflect:
   - ins: bits [7:5] of first instruction register
   - ad1: bits [4:0] of first instruction register
   - ad2: complete second instruction register value

Assume all changes to inputs occur synchronous to the clock edge.
QUESTION END
