   a. Rotate the stored value left by 1 bit (MSB moves to LSB position)
   b. Output the current MSB on dout
   c. Keep valid_out low

The serial output should maintain the original bit order of the input data (MSB first) and repeat this pattern continuously. Assume the input d remains stable during the 4-cycle period.

Example:
If input d = 4'b1101, the output sequence would be:
Cycle 0: dout=1, valid_out=1 (load new data)
Cycle 1: dout=1 (rotated to 4'b1011)
Cycle 2: dout=0 (rotated to 4'b0111)
Cycle 3: dout=1 (rotated to 4'b1110)
Cycle 4: dout=1, valid_out=1 (load new data)
...and so on.
QUESTION END
