Design a clock divider module that generates three derived clock signals from a single input clock. The module should have the following specifications:

Inputs:
- CLK_in: Primary input clock signal
- RST: Active-high synchronous reset

Outputs:
- CLK_50: Clock signal with exactly half the frequency of CLK_in (50% duty cycle)
- CLK_10: Clock signal with 1/10th the frequency of CLK_in (50% duty cycle)
- CLK_1: Clock signal with 1/100th the frequency of CLK_in (50% duty cycle)

Behavior:
1. All outputs should reset to 0 when RST is high
2. All outputs should toggle on rising edges of CLK_in when not in reset
3. CLK_50 should toggle every input clock cycle
4. CLK_10 should toggle every 5 input clock cycles (10 half-cycles)
5. CLK_1 should toggle every 50 input clock cycles (100 half-cycles)
6. All outputs must maintain a 50% duty cycle

Assume all signals are 1-bit values. The implementation must use only positive-edge triggered flip-flops and synchronous reset behavior.
QUESTION END
