Design a parameterized dual-clock synchronous RAM module with separate read and write interfaces. The module should support:

1. Write Interface:
   - Clock: wclk (positive edge triggered)
   - Enable: wenc (active high)
   - Address: waddr (width automatically calculated from DEPTH)
   - Data: wdata (width specified by WIDTH parameter)

2. Read Interface:
   - Clock: rclk (positive edge triggered, independent of wclk)
   - Enable: renc (active high)
   - Address: raddr (same width as waddr)
   - Data: rdata (registered output, same width as wdata)

Parameters:
- DEPTH: Number of memory locations (default 16)
- WIDTH: Data width in bits (default 8)

Behavior:
- Writes occur on wclk rising edge when wenc is high
- Reads occur on rclk rising edge when renc is high
- Read and write operations are completely independent
- Address widths should be automatically calculated to support DEPTH

The module should correctly handle concurrent read/write operations to different addresses. Do not include any reset functionality.
QUESTION END
