   - Read operation occurs on rclk posedge when rinc is high and FIFO is not empty
   - Reset (active low) clears all pointers and flags
   - Full/empty flags must be properly synchronized between clock domains
   - The FIFO should correctly handle all corner cases (full, empty, simultaneous read/write)

The implementation must use gray code pointers for reliable cross-clock domain synchronization and include appropriate synchronization stages. The FIFO should be parameterizable for different widths and depths while maintaining correct functionality.
