Design an asynchronous FIFO (First-In-First-Out) buffer with the following specifications:

1. Interface:
   - Write clock (wclk) and read clock (rclk) - independent clock domains
   - Active-low write reset (wrstn) and read reset (rrstn)
   - Write enable (winc) and read enable (rinc) signals
   - WIDTH-bit input data (wdata) and output data (rdata)
   - Full flag (wfull) and empty flag (rempty) outputs

2. Parameters:
   - WIDTH: Data width (default 8 bits)
   - DEPTH: FIFO depth (default 16 entries)

3. Behavior:
   - The FIFO must safely transfer data between asynchronous clock domains
   - Write operation occurs on wclk rising edge when winc is high and FIFO is not full
   - Read operation occurs on rclk rising edge when rinc is high and FIFO is not empty
   - wfull should be asserted when the FIFO is full (prevent overflow)
   - rempty should be asserted when the FIFO is empty (prevent underflow)
   - Reset should clear all pointers and flags synchronously in each clock domain

4. Implementation Requirements:
   - Use Gray code for pointer synchronization between clock domains
   - Properly handle metastability in cross-domain signals
   - Calculate required address width based on DEPTH parameter
   - Include parameterized instantiation of a memory array (do not implement the memory itself)

The solution should correctly handle all edge cases including simultaneous read/write operations and reset conditions.
QUESTION END
