Inputs:
- a, b: 32-bit input operands
- aluc: 6-bit control signal specifying the operation to perform

Outputs:
- r: 32-bit result of the operation
- zero: 1 when result equals zero
- carry: carry/borrow output for arithmetic operations (MSB of 33-bit intermediate result)
- negative: 1 when result is negative (MSB of result)
- overflow: 1 when signed arithmetic overflow occurs
- flag: comparison result for SLT/SLTU operations, high-Z otherwise

Supported Operations:
The ALU should implement the following operations (control codes given as comments):
- ADD/ADDU: Signed/unsigned addition
- SUB/SUBU: Signed/unsigned subtraction
- AND/OR/XOR/NOR: Bitwise logical operations
- SLT/SLTU: Set if less than (signed/unsigned)
- SLL/SRL/SRA: Shift operations (logical/arithmetic)
- SLLV/SRLV/SRAV: Variable shift operations
- LUI: Load upper immediate (shift left by 16 bits)

Timing:
- The output should update combinationally when any input changes
- All outputs should be valid within the same clock cycle

Additional Requirements:
- Handle signed operations correctly using two's complement
- For shift operations, use the lower 5 bits of the shift amount
- The flag output should only be valid for comparison operations (SLT/SLTU)
