Design an 8-bit data processing module that transforms input data based on a 3-bit control signal. The module should have the following interface:

Inputs:
- in[7:0]: 8-bit input data
- ctrl[2:0]: 3-bit control signal

Output:
- out[7:0]: 8-bit transformed output

The transformation occurs in three stages, with each stage controlled by one bit of the control signal (ctrl[2] controls stage 1, ctrl[1] stage 2, and ctrl[0] stage 3). Each stage performs bit-level operations as follows:

Stage 1 (controlled by ctrl[2]):
- When ctrl[2] is 0: Pass bits [7:0] through unchanged
- When ctrl[2] is 1: 
  - Set bits [7:4] to 0
  - Replace bits [3:0] with bits [7:4] of the input

Stage 2 (controlled by ctrl[1]):
- When ctrl[1] is 0: Pass bits [7:0] through unchanged
- When ctrl[1] is 1:
  - Set bits [7:6] to 0
  - Replace bits [5:0] with bits [7:2] of the stage 1 output

Stage 3 (controlled by ctrl[0]):
- When ctrl[0] is 0: Pass bits [7:0] through unchanged
- When ctrl[0] is 1:
  - Set bit [7] to 0
  - Replace bits [6:0] with bits [7:1] of the stage 2 output

The output should reflect the cumulative effect of all three stages. Each stage's output becomes the input to the next stage. The transformation should be purely combinational with no clock or reset signals.
