   - Output proper signed results (negative if inputs have opposite signs)
   - Assert 'res_valid' when result is ready and keep it asserted until 'res_ready' is high
   - Remain idle until new operation is requested

3. Timing:
   - All inputs sampled on rising clock edge
   - New operation can only start when no division is in progress
   - Result appears 8 cycles after operation starts
   - Output remains valid until acknowledged by 'res_ready'

Assume divisor is never zero. The module should handle backpressure properly using the valid/ready handshake protocol.
