1. Write Interface:
   - Clock: wclk (positive edge triggered)
   - Enable: wenc (active high)
   - Address: waddr (width automatically calculated from DEPTH)
   - Data: wdata (width specified by WIDTH parameter)

2. Read Interface:
   - Clock: rclk (positive edge triggered)
   - Enable: renc (active high)
   - Address: raddr (same width as waddr)
   - Output: rdata (same width as wdata)

The module should have two parameters:
- DEPTH: Number of memory locations (default 16)
- WIDTH: Data width in bits (default 8)

Functionality:
- Write operations occur on wclk rising edge when wenc is high
- Read operations occur on rclk rising edge when renc is high
- Reads and writes are completely independent (can occur simultaneously)
- Read data should be registered (output changes only on rclk edges)

Assume all inputs are properly synchronized to their respective clocks. The address inputs should automatically scale based on DEPTH (use $clog2).
QUESTION END
