   - Enable: renc (active high)
   - Address: raddr (same width as waddr)
   - Data: rdata (registered output, same width as wdata)

The module should have two parameters:
- DEPTH: Number of memory locations (default 16)
- WIDTH: Data width in bits (default 8)

Key requirements:
- Writes occur synchronously to wclk when wenc is high
- Reads occur synchronously to rclk when renc is high
- Read and write operations are completely independent
- Address widths should be automatically calculated from DEPTH
- All signals must be properly registered

Assume all inputs are valid (no need for error checking). The memory should be initialized to undefined values.
QUESTION END
