Design a synchronous FIFO (First-In-First-Out) buffer that operates across two clock domains. The FIFO should support simultaneous read and write operations with proper full/empty status flags to prevent overflow and underflow conditions.

The module should have the following specifications:

1. Interface:
   - Write clock (wclk) and read clock (rclk) - asynchronous clocks
   - Active-low write reset (wrstn) and read reset (rrstn)
   - Write enable (winc) and read enable (rinc) signals
   - Write data input (wdata) with configurable WIDTH (default 8 bits)
   - Read data output (rdata) of same width as input
   - Full flag (wfull) - asserted when FIFO is full
   - Empty flag (rempty) - asserted when FIFO is empty

2. Behavior:
   - Write operations occur on wclk rising edge when winc is high and FIFO is not full
   - Read operations occur on rclk rising edge when rinc is high and FIFO is not empty
   - The FIFO depth should be configurable via DEPTH parameter (default 16)
   - Proper synchronization of pointers between clock domains to avoid metastability
   - Reset should clear all pointers and status flags

3. Implementation Constraints:
   - Use Gray code for pointer synchronization between clock domains
   - The actual storage element implementation is provided (dut submodule)
   - Status flags must be properly synchronized to their respective clock domains

The solution should correctly handle all edge cases including simultaneous read/write operations when the FIFO is nearly full or empty.
QUESTION END
