Design a clock domain crossing (CDC) FIFO module with the following specifications:

1. Interface:
   - Write clock (wclk) and read clock (rclk) - asynchronous clocks
   - Active-low write reset (wrstn) and read reset (rrstn)
   - Write enable (winc) and read enable (rinc) signals
   - Data input (wdata) with configurable width (WIDTH parameter)
   - Data output (rdata) with same width as input
   - Full flag (wfull) and empty flag (rempty) outputs

2. Functionality:
   - The FIFO should have configurable depth (DEPTH parameter)
   - Implement proper clock domain crossing for all control signals
   - Write operations occur on wclk rising edge when winc is high and FIFO isn't full
   - Read operations occur on rclk rising edge when rinc is high and FIFO isn't empty
   - wfull should be asserted when FIFO is full (write domain)
   - rempty should be asserted when FIFO is empty (read domain)
   - Use Gray code encoding for CDC synchronization
   - All resets should be asynchronous and active-low

3. Parameters:
   - WIDTH: Data width in bits (default 8)
   - DEPTH: FIFO depth in words (default 16, must be power of 2)

The module should correctly handle all CDC scenarios and maintain data integrity during simultaneous read/write operations across clock domains. Do not implement the actual memory array - assume it's provided as a blackbox submodule.
QUESTION END
