Inputs:
- CLK_in: Primary input clock signal
- RST: Active-high synchronous reset

Outputs:
- CLK_50: Clock signal with exactly half the frequency of CLK_in (50% duty cycle)
- CLK_10: Clock signal with 1/10th the frequency of CLK_in (50% duty cycle)
- CLK_1: Clock signal with 1/100th the frequency of CLK_in (50% duty cycle)

Requirements:
1. All output clocks must be synchronous to the rising edge of CLK_in
2. All output clocks must reset to 0 when RST is asserted
3. The CLK_50 output should toggle on every rising edge of CLK_in
4. The CLK_10 output should toggle every 5 cycles of CLK_in (after counting 0-4)
5. The CLK_1 output should toggle every 50 cycles of CLK_in (after counting 0-49)
6. All counters must reset to 0 when RST is asserted

Assume all signals are 1-bit unless otherwise specified. The module should be purely synchronous with no asynchronous logic except for the reset.
QUESTION END
