Design a 32-bit Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU) module that performs various arithmetic and logical operations based on a 6-bit control signal. The ALU should support both signed and unsigned operations with appropriate status flag outputs.

Inputs:
- a, b: 32-bit operands
- aluc: 6-bit operation control code

Outputs:
- r: 32-bit result
- zero: high when result equals zero
- carry: high when operation produces carry-out (for arithmetic ops)
- negative: high when result is negative (for signed ops)
- overflow: high when signed arithmetic overflow occurs
- flag: special comparison result for SLT/SLTU ops, high-Z otherwise

The ALU should support the following operations (aluc values in parentheses):
- Arithmetic: ADD (100000), ADDU (100001), SUB (100010), SUBU (100011)
- Logical: AND (100100), OR (100101), XOR (100110), NOR (100111)
- Comparisons: SLT (101010), SLTU (101011)
- Shifts: SLL (000000), SRL (000010), SRA (000011), SLLV (000100), SRLV (000110), SRAV (000111)
- Special: LUI (001111)

For arithmetic operations, generate appropriate status flags. For SLT/SLTU operations, set flag to the comparison result (1 if true, 0 otherwise) and keep it high-Z for other operations. The zero flag should be set for all operations except JR. All outputs should update combinationally when any input changes.

Note: Signed operations should use two's complement representation. Shift amounts should be taken from the lower 5 bits of operand a for variable shifts.
QUESTION END
